A||||9||88formula||Which injectors for a 3.4 fiero||||1||
Z||000000||88formula||09-02-2000||11:00 PM||||I am trying to figure out which injectors I should use for my 3.4-liter Camaro engine. I have blueprinted 2.8 injectors from Marren Motorsports and the 3.4 injectors that I could use right now. What do you guys use with your 3.4 engines?<P>My engine is going to have the GM 3.4 crate engine cam (12363220) and a 9.8 to 1 compression ratio.<P>I would also like advice on a custom prom chip. Any advice would be appreciated.<P>Thanks<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||tgowens||09-03-2000||02:47 AM||||we (Fiero Shop) sell the Lucas injector for a 305 motor and find it far superior to anything else in the 3.4. call us at 510-23-FIERO (510-233-4376)<P>------------------<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/Terry_sig.gif">                    <BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero" TARGET=_blank>www.tgowens.com/fiero</A><BR>Gold '87 GT<BR>Blue '87 GT||||reg||1
Z||000002||fierocrazy||09-04-2000||05:23 PM||||my tech told me 2.8 to 3.4 are all the same, So I used 3.8 in my 2.8 block my.o2||||reg||1
Z||000003||88formula||09-04-2000||05:46 PM||||I have both 3.4 & 2.8 injectors in my hand and physically they are different. The 3.4 has sequential fuel injection (one at a time) and the 2.8 has Port fuel injection (batch fire). They can't be the same.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Old Lar||09-04-2000||08:34 PM||||According to the 3.4 conversion that Twin Lakes Fiero does, Bob's sheet says new high performance fuel injectors.  What does that mean..Check with Fierobob.||||reg||1
Z||000005||88formula||09-04-2000||08:55 PM||||Who is fierobob?<P>Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000006||Alex4mula||09-05-2000||03:57 PM||||88formula; Just like you I had my 2.8 injectors blue printed by Marren. Becasue of that I used them in my 3.4 before investing in others. I haven't been able to prove problems with the 2.8 ones but if I were you I would use the 3.4 ones. They may look different (& they are) but they have the right impedance for the computer. You may need a new chip if they flow 10% to 15% more fuel. I'm not sure about the exact lbs/hr spec for both. Hope this help.||||reg||1
Z||000007||88formula||09-05-2000||05:17 PM||||I think I will try the 3.4 injectors first. Did you have to turn your fuel pressure up with the 2.8 injectors?<p>[This message has been edited by 88formula (edited 09-05-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||Alex4mula||09-05-2000||07:19 PM||||I have tried several presures but with the seat of the pants measurement method I didn't feel big differences. It feels ok from 38 to 45 psi. O2 readings don't show lean condition. Injector pulse runs 10ms to 11ms at WOT. Need to take it to dyno shop and see if they do an A/F analysis. Haven't have the time  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> ...||||reg||1
Z||000009||terryk||09-05-2000||11:26 PM||||I recommend the 3.4L injectors but nothing bigger. The bigger injectors are difficult to control at low pulse widths (meaning idle). The 2.8L injectors will flow plenty up in the 3.4L area, but the 3.4L injectors will give you a bit of room. <P>I assume these are SFI injectors and not DOHC injectors, right?<P>And find a scanner to borrow.....<p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 09-05-2000).]||||reg||12
